  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of inky fog within range. The fog is magical &amp;Reference[darkness apply=false]{Darkness} and lasts for the duration, or until a strong wind (such as the one created by @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplGustofWind]{Gust of Wind}) disperses it, ending the spell.</p><p>Each creature in the Sphere when it appears makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, it takes 5d6 Psychic damage and subtracts 1d6 from its saving throws until the end of its next turn; on a success, it takes half as much damage only. A creature also makes this save when the Sphere moves into its space, when it enters the Sphere, or when it ends its turn inside, no more than once per turn.</p><p>The Sphere moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns.</p><p><strong>Casting as a Circle Spell.</strong> Casting it as a Circle spell requires at least five secondary casters. The spell’s range becomes 1 mile, and its duration becomes until dispelled (no Concentration required). The spell ends early if any caster who took part contributes to another casting of Doomtide as a Circle spell. In addition to the spell’s usual components, you must provide a special component (a string of three black pearls from Pandemonium), which the spell consumes. When the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 3+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
